how to get over the fear of public  speaking if you're an expert in your  field and you should be as an  entrepreneur then public speaking will  become a part of what you do you you  want to be the face of your company you  want to be able to promote yourself  properly how people be able to spread  your message and it's a part of your  responsibility is to be able to do great  media interviews and be able to do  presentations to spread your work I got  a great question from one of my readers  siddell who wrote in to say I need tips  to get over my fear of public speaking  and deliver a great presentation I know  it's scary anything you do for the first  time is scary especially when there's a  peep a group of people watching you and  you know there's an opportunity to fail  and suck and and worry about how people  are gonna think about you it's one thing  to fail on your own where nobody can see  but failing in public where people can  watch that's scary that adds a whole  other level to things that that makes it  a lot harder to get into but it is a  skill that you can learn just like  anything else and you can become a lot  more comfortable with it I remember one  of my presentations one of my first kind  of big presentations I was flown to  Brunei after I'd sold my software  company to help teach their young  entrepreneurs how to be successful as  entrepreneurs and I was shocked to find  out that it was a huge room there are  500 people there I was up on a big stage  and it was being broadcast nationally on  their television station I had done that  many presentations up to that point so I  was sweating bullets I was really  nervous but but what really helps me  through through that and through every  presentation it wasn't things like  imagine people in their underwear  imagine you talking to your family I  don't know I read a lot of this stuff  none of that helped me if that works for  you go for it but for me it didn't work  what helped me was number one  remembering why I'm doing this and this  isn't just for speaking this is for  anything that makes you nervous if you  are going into a sales call if you're  hiring your first employee whenever you  start something new that you haven't  done before you're gonna be a little  scared and nervous about it but remember  why you're doing is you're getting up on  stage to do a presentation why are you  there and it should be to help people  right if it's not to help people then  you shouldn't be doing  you're not gonna get a great result your  goal going up on stage and doing that  presentation is to help the audience  realize something to help them make a  change in their lives for the better so  it's a noble goal it's something that  you're up there to help you're not up  there to pitch or this Sal and I've  always found that helpful for me even  even not so much now but but when I  started my business I'm a chemical comm  I got nervous talking to big companies  you know Microsoft will call me and say  we want to work with you and it gets so  nervous before the call I call got a  call in an hour at Microsoft when we're  gonna say I don't look stupid I want to  I want to showcase my expertise and what  I'm talking about  hope you don't say the wrong thing I got  so nervous I built up this whole thing  in my head this block and I realized  like these guys I can help them I know I  could help them this isn't something  that that I'm not sure if I can do or  not I know I can help them I know I can  help them get results and so that calms  me and again this works for me I don't  know if it works for you but but it  works for me so I think about my  audience and I know I can help them  stand in front of this camera and  speaking to you guys it's a little less  nerve-wracking than being on stage but  but I do it more confidently because I  know I can help and that's my intention  it's not to sell you on my worksheets or  my website or my business or anything  it's to help you help answer this  question and so that can be a great goal  going in the second thing that I found  really useful for me is practice just  like any other skill you want to learn  you want to learn how to do something  you have to practice and you start small  and sometimes the end goal may be maybe  so big it may be so unattainable because  you don't know the steps to get there  and if you want to learn how to  snowboard you may look at some of the  great snowboarders and they're doing all  these tricks and flips and and you can't  even stand up on your board and you  think that's impossible I'm never gonna  get there right if you look at speakers  and you look at Tony Robbins or whoever  your favorite speaker is and you see how  great he is and and you think I'm never  gonna be like that and so you don't get  started because you're too afraid you  can be great but you have to start at  the beginning you start you start  sucking you start but you start  and you start getting better each time  you get better and better and better and  it may be at the beginning just doing it  in front of a camera we're just doing it  in front of the mirror I did so many  presentations as my practice just  talking to myself in the mirror that's  what I did and it helped it gave me  confidence that I'd gone through it a  couple times I knew what I was talking  about I got comfortable material more  and more my wear my jokes are gonna be  all of that and it made the presentation  better so talk to yourself in the mirror  record some of your videos  I'm new gonna play them back and think  they were terrible and you're gonna be  your own worst critic I still look back  on my first YouTube videos and think oh  my god these are so bad I should I  should remove them they're they're  really bad by my standards now but  people still like them and watch them  and it's fun to see that the progression  so I keep them up but record yourself  put it up start doing speaking at small  events so some of the first speaking of  gigs that I did were at the YMCA were at  my local city government they had these  workshops for entrepreneurs that I  delivered all of that helped and there  were small groups you know my first  presentation were three people who  showed up three people and then I had  five and then I had ten and then I had  20 and it started to grow and as you  start doing something and you achieve a  little bit of success you get some  confidence like if you can get to here  you thought getting here would be really  hard but you got there you did it now I  said I can do that I'm okay doing that  and now you can push yourself to go here  and then here and you slowly make your  way up and soon you're at the point  where you couldn't imagine that you  would get that far because you've gotten  so much practice you've gotten so much  better and you enjoy it so start start  small start talking to yourself start  making video start putting them up get  your practice do something every day if  your goal is to be a public speaker do  something every day to practice being a  public speaker and that could be going  to an advantage speaking or could be on  your own recording yourself in your in  your home in your office I used to get  nervous recording myself when there are  people around the first step was me  being nervous just in front of the  camera  and and I could say great when I wasn't  on camera but then I got the camera and  I started stuttering and  I'm you know my it's not making sense  but then I could get comfortable enough  to do it on my own but if somebody was  in the room with me I would panic you  know I would stumble I get nervous I  start sweating and it wouldn't it  wouldn't flow wouldn't come out now I  can do that and it's not a problem but  it just it comes to practice and each  time you get a little better and a  little butter and a little bitter like  any other muscle you build it up and you  get stronger so I know it's scary at the  start I know it can be overwhelming I  know there's a huge fear of making  yourself look stupid and and falling on  your face in front of in front of other  people right that's a huge fear but if  you can remember why you're doing this  and it's a noble goal and you want to  help people and and this is something  that you're set out to do and you  practice and practice and practice on  your own in front of the camera in front  of small audiences and you start to  build it up you'll get better and better  and better and you'll keep improving  your quality and you eventually get to  be the person that you looked up to if  it was 20 Roberts or whoever it is you  can get to that level to practice belief  for those of you watching if you like  the video please give it a thumbs up  below it always makes me want to do more  for you if you have a comment about this  video a tip you have and how to be a  good public speaker or if you have  another question for your business leave  it below I'm a good video response thank  you so much and I'll see you soon  you
 

